Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.37,0:00:04.69,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Now film the trajectory,\None frame every two time units.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.14,0:00:07.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Neighbouring frames look alike.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.65,0:00:09.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Cut the film into frames.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.66,0:00:14.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Drop them in a shoebox, shake,\Nand throw away the timestamps.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.69,0:00:19.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Pour the box out:\Nthe frames redraw the same glow.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.79,0:00:24.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Each frame is a snapshot:\Nthree dial readings, nothing more.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.35,0:00:27.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}It carries no timestamp and no time order.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:27.66,0:00:31.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Yet the shoebox, plus the equations,\Nanswers many questions.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.07,0:00:37.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Averages, energy budgets, even\Nhow often the dipole crosses zero.
